  "worked_solution": "The function $y={f}^{-1}(x)$ is a reflection of $y=f(x)$ in the line $y=x.$ Therefore, each point $(a,b)$ on $y=f(x)$ has a corresponding point $(b,a)$ on $y={f}^{-1}(x)$ (the $x$ and $y$ coordinates swap).\n\nSince the point $(-4,\\sqrt{3})$ lies on $y=f(x),$ the point $(\\sqrt{3},-4)$ lies on $y={f}^{-1}(x).$",
